From d00aa6b3e84431afa9c8c429e37ffd73607706f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marius Gehrmann <marius@gehrmann.solutions>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 17:16:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 18/22] drm: apple: Say that a waiting Type-C display takes
 over by itself

The log line for a Type-C display that waits for a pipeline told the
user to unplug the other display and then plug this one in again. A
waiting display does not need that: when the other display goes, the
fabric hands the pipeline to the waiting port (dcp_typec_route_waiting()),
and on J613 it came up by itself in every test, from either port, about
2.5 s after the other display was unplugged. With the lid closed, the
internal pipe takes it over by itself as well.

Say what happens:

  display on USB-C Left-front waits for an external display pipeline:
  it drives another display; unplug that one and this one takes over

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017YMqWu7A3VwEYtHaA1TusK
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-fabric.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-fabric.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-fabric.c
index 5b6960153..cfd69f4c0 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-fabric.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-fabric.c
@@ -1266,7 +1266,7 @@ static int dcp_typec_port_busy(struct apple_dcp_typec_port *port,
 	port->busy_noted = true;
 	of_property_read_string(port->connector_np, "label", &label);
 	dev_info(dcp->dev,
-		 "display on %s waits for an external display pipeline: it drives another display; to switch, unplug that one, then plug this one in again\n",
+		 "display on %s waits for an external display pipeline: it drives another display; unplug that one and this one takes over\n",
 		 label ?: "a USB-C port");
 	return -EBUSY;
 }
